{"agent":"pperf2","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`sparkline` does not scale to `width` unless every finite value is identical. For `[0, 1, 2, 3, 4]` and `width=2` it returns five glyphs (`▁▂▄▆█`), not two cells, so a caller that trusts the docstring and the terminal width bound gets an over-wide line. The same path also drops `None` (`[1.0, None, 3.0]` becomes two blocks), so a missing sample disappears instead of staying unavailable. Only the flat case uses `width` (`_SPARK[0] * width`).","digest":"8e7afbcbcc661465","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:sparkline","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:sparkline"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"An empty comparison is still emitted as a header with no rows and no `n/a` / `not collected`. Given `comparisons` of `{\"models\": [], \"reviewers\": [], \"agents\": []}` (or missing keys, which `.get` turns into `[]`), `render` always appends `model        pass`, `reviewer        pass`, and `agent        pass`. That is an empty section, which this module’s own contract says must not be rendered as a blank table.","digest":"7de5a916bc4c6193","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:_comparison","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:_comparison"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"There is no size knob, stated cut, or next call. `render` walks every gate and every comparison row; 1000 gates produce 1000 table lines plus headers, with only per-line ellipsis from `_clip`. Nothing records that the answer was cut or names the CLI/MCP call for the rest. `sparkline` is also never used, so the report text has no trend sparkline at all. `_clip` itself is not a bound for `width < 2`: `width=0` and `\"abc\"` yields `\"ab…\"` (length 3).","digest":"a7307fe681ea4099","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:render","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:render"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":9276,"diff_sha":"10476ce7c5ff6a91320d93e11a99efa552ae3234b64f71c2b1e9cae89d240cb7","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/PM-report-text","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":50.2,"family":"xai","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"e6bd2cc83d6ac68d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/PM-report-text.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261110T033948Z-0f9ae5fa.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"7d89650294c01b4695cb23b875449096b2488764","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py":"100644 900591b40ba9f5f5c61ff9a3f66221cc70dd3e3d","tests/test_perf_render_text.py":"100644 2b4f6d34da52c02514672e73460d3ef7e6e481b4"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:sparkline","ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:_comparison","ddflow/services/perf/render_text.py:render"],"tree_sha":"7d89650294c0+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"ee3540cd4f94de79b6423a037","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":165334,"schema":1,"subject":"PM-report-text","ts":"2026-11-10T03:40:39.001944Z"}
